@startuml consumer-outage-recovery
title US-08: Consumer Outage Recovery - Kafka Retains Events Until Consumer Returns

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Ingestion\nPoller" as Poller
queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer

Poller -> Kafka : publishing raw events continuously

note over Consumer
  Consumer goes down.
  Offset is committed up to last
  successfully processed event.
end note

Consumer ->x Consumer : crash / restart

Poller -> Kafka : events continue to accumulate
Poller -> Kafka : events continue to accumulate
Poller -> Kafka : events continue to accumulate

note over Kafka
  Events are retained on disk
  for the configured retention window.
  No events are lost while
  the consumer is down.
end note

Consumer -> Consumer : restart

Consumer -> Kafka : resume from last committed offset
Kafka --> Consumer : replay all missed events in order

note over Consumer
  Consumer catches up at its
  own processing speed.
  Idempotency key on every write
  makes replay safe. (US-11)
end note

Consumer -> Consumer : offset caught up - processing live events

@enduml
